From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: report CPE and client association uptime

Use an RDK vendor-specific metrics extension to carry an agent's monotonic
boot uptime and each associated station's current-association uptime.  The
controller converts device uptime to a stable boot epoch, persists that value
without updating the database on every metrics interval, and exposes live
elapsed values through the existing network and STA models.

The CLI presents CPE uptime and client association uptime.  Controller uptime
comes from local /proc/uptime; all other nodes come from the reporting agent.
Association uptime resets on disconnect or roam.  Also label the currently
unpopulated device signal field accurately as backhaul signal instead of
presenting a generic N/A value as though a standard node-wide RSSI existed.

This is an RDK vendor extension.  EasyMesh standard AP Metrics remain the
source of client RCPI; no proprietary replacement is introduced for them.

Upstream-Status: Pending

